guide.kg.name.guide_quick_start=Six-step grill flow
guide.kg.body.guide_quick_start.1=Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.guide_quick_start.2=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total.
guide.kg.body.guide_quick_start.3=After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill.
guide.kg.body.guide_quick_start.4=After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.name.guide_grill=Grill controls
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.1=A grill holds up to 3 skewers. New raw skewers can only be inserted while it is lit, still unoiled, and has a free slot.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.2=Flint and Steel lights it; vanilla shovels or the Cookery Kitchen Shovel can extinguish it.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.3=Brushing uses a filled Cookery Oil Pot and consumes one oil point for each skewer currently on the grill.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.4=An empty hand flips or extracts. Holding an unrelated item will not silently advance the grill stage.
guide.kg.name.guide_grill_timing=Timing, overcooking & burning
guide.kg.body.guide_grill_timing.1=Whenever the grill is lit and occupied, the current stage is timed. Brushing or a successful flip starts a fresh stage timer.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill_timing.2=If a stage is not advanced for about 40 seconds, the skewers become overcooked; they can still be extracted as Dark Grilling.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill_timing.3=Keep an overcooked batch heating for about 20 more seconds and it burns into charcoal.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill_timing.4=If you need to stop, extinguish the grill with a shovel. Timers do not advance while it is unlit.
guide.kg.name.guide_threading=Hand threading
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.1=Hold a stick or unfinished skewer in the off hand and a skewerable ingredient in the main hand, then use it to add ingredients one at a time.
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.2=A skewer holds at most 3 ingredients. A matching fixed recipe resolves immediately; three ingredients that do not match a fixed recipe become a Secret Skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.3=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.guide_plate=Skewer Plate
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.1=A Skewer Plate stores up to 5 skewers. Use a skewer on it to add one; use an empty hand to remove the most recently inserted skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.2=Eating from a plate with several skewers consumes the one with the highest base nutrition first.
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.3=A non-empty plate can be sneak-placed, and its stored skewer data is preserved when carried again.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_book=Skewer Recipe Book
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.1=Use an empty Skewer Recipe Book in the main hand with a complete raw skewer in the off hand to record a fixed or complete Secret recipe without consuming the skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.2=Use a recorded book with a stick in the off hand to pull each ingredient from inventory. Missing ingredients do not cause a partial craft.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.3=A recorded book can be placed on a horizontal block face; use a stick on the wall recipe to quick-craft the same way.
guide.kg.name.guide_oil_press=Oil Press
guide.kg.body.guide_oil_press.1=First make Oil Cake: surround 1 Wheat with 8 Canola Powder. The Oil Press must be loaded with all 4 cakes before pressing.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil_press.2=A batch needs 16 progress: an anvil adds 4; Stone, Cobblestone, Deepslate, Cobbled Deepslate, or Blackstone adds 1 per press.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil_press.3=A completed batch produces 4 buckets of Canola Oil and 4 Oil Residue, but a nearby Big Vat must be able to accept all 4 buckets at once.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil_press.4=If no vat is available, it is full, or it contains another fluid, the press waits. Fix the container and interact again to retry.
guide.kg.name.guide_big_vat=Big Vat
guide.kg.body.guide_big_vat.1=A Big Vat holds 8 buckets and only one fluid type at a time: water, lava, Canola Oil, Secret Chili Oil, or Premium Chili Oil.
guide.kg.body.guide_big_vat.2=Use the matching bucket to fill or extract it; use an empty hand to view its current fluid and bucket count.
guide.kg.body.guide_big_vat.3=The three Grilling oils can fill a Cookery Oil Pot directly: each vat bucket adds 8 oil points.
guide.kg.body.guide_big_vat.4=Breaking a filled vat preserves its fluid type and amount on the dropped vat item; placing it again restores the contents.
guide.kg.name.guide_advanced_rack=Advanced Kitchen Rack
guide.kg.body.guide_advanced_rack.1=The Advanced Kitchen Rack has 9 slots: the first 5 are for oil pots/seasoning bottles, and the last 4 are for kitchen knives, the kitchen shovel, Flint and Steel, and similar tools.
guide.kg.body.guide_advanced_rack.2=The first inserted item establishes a slot filter. Oil-pot states share one family, and empty/pending/special seasoning bottles share one family.
guide.kg.body.guide_advanced_rack.3=Open the rack to swap with the selected hotbar slot, deposit, withdraw, or clear an empty-slot filter. Deposit All follows existing filters.
guide.kg.body.guide_advanced_rack.4=Use range is 8 blocks. Breaking the rack stores its contents and filters on the dropped item, which are restored when placed again.
guide.kg.name.guide_crops=Crop overview
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.1=Grilling currently grows Canola, Houttuynia, Onion, and Sweet Potato. Mature crops feed into processing chains rather than being only direct food.
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.2=Canola is mainly for oil; Onion mills into Onion Powder; Sweet Potato becomes powder/sheets; Houttuynia can be chopped for skewers and dishes.
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.3=Oil Residue can be used on crops with growth stages to advance their growth further.
guide.kg.name.guide_canola=Canola to oil
guide.kg.body.guide_canola.1=Mill Canola Seeds in the Cookery Millstone to obtain Canola Powder.
guide.kg.body.guide_canola.2=At a crafting table, surround 1 Wheat with 8 Canola Powder to make 1 Oil Cake; 4 cakes make one press batch.
guide.kg.body.guide_canola.3=A completed Oil Press batch transfers 4 buckets of Canola Oil into a suitable nearby Big Vat and ejects 4 Oil Residue.
guide.kg.name.guide_houttuynia=Houttuynia processing
guide.kg.body.guide_houttuynia.1=Chop Houttuynia 4 times on a Cookery Chopping Board to make Minced Houttuynia; the Sweet Potato Sheet Skewer uses the minced ingredient.
guide.kg.body.guide_houttuynia.2=Whole Houttuynia also participates in dishes such as Cold Houttuynia; see Advanced & Troubleshooting for the Premium Chili Oil interaction.
guide.kg.body.guide_houttuynia.3=Houttuynia Powder extends Special Seasoning effects; see Seasoning & Hot Food for the exact multipliers.
guide.kg.name.guide_sweet_potato=Sweet Potato & sheets
guide.kg.body.guide_sweet_potato.1=Mill Sweet Potato in the Cookery Millstone to obtain Sweet Potato Powder.
guide.kg.body.guide_sweet_potato.2=Cut Sweet Potato Powder 4 times on a Cookery Chopping Board to make Raw Sweet Potato Sheet, or hold-use the powder for about 1.5 seconds to knead it directly.
guide.kg.body.guide_sweet_potato.3=Sweet Potato can also be cooked in a furnace, smoker, campfire, or soul campfire into Roasted Sweet Potato, which grants about 30 seconds of Warmth.
guide.kg.name.guide_cutting=Common skewer prep
guide.kg.body.guide_cutting.1=Cut a Carrot 4 times on a Cookery Chopping Board to get 3 Carrot Dice.
guide.kg.body.guide_cutting.2=Cut a Potato 4 times to get 3 Potato Slices.
guide.kg.body.guide_cutting.3=Cut a Cookery Mantou 4 times to get 3 Raw Mantou Slices. Cookery Red Chili can instead be milled into Red Chili Powder.
guide.kg.name.guide_chicken_processing=Chicken Skin & Wings
guide.kg.body.guide_chicken_processing.1=Finish the 4-cut raw-chicken process on a Cookery Chopping Board with a kitchen knife to receive extra Chicken Skin.
guide.kg.body.guide_chicken_processing.2=Killing a chicken with a Cookery kitchen knife drops Chicken Wings; Looting can increase the amount.
guide.kg.body.guide_chicken_processing.3=Chicken Skin and Chicken Wings both feed into fixed skewer recipes.
guide.kg.name.guide_pepper_tree=Sichuan Pepper Tree
guide.kg.body.guide_pepper_tree.1=Plant a Sichuan Pepper Sapling on a dirt-like block. At light level 9 or higher it can grow randomly, and Bone Meal can also attempt to advance growth.
guide.kg.body.guide_pepper_tree.2=Use an empty hand on fruiting leaves to harvest 1–2 Sichuan Pepper, returning the leaves to an unfruited state.
guide.kg.body.guide_pepper_tree.3=Pepper leaves sting: stepping on them briefly slows and damages entities, except foxes and bees.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_base=Making Special Seasoning
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_base.1=Place an Empty Seasoning Bottle and add ingredients to the top bottle. Each bottle stores up to 8 ingredients, and up to 4 bottles can be stacked in the world.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_base.2=A finished seasoning requires at least one Green Chili Powder, one Sichuan Pepper, and one Onion Powder. Once all three bases are present, it becomes Seasoning to Be Shaken.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_base.3=Take the pending bottle back with an empty hand and hold-use/shake it to finish Special Seasoning. A finished bottle has 16 uses.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_base.4=Seasoning a grill costs 1 use per skewer currently on the grill; insufficient remaining uses do not partially commit.
guide.kg.name.guide_hot_food=Hot Food & the three oils
guide.kg.body.guide_hot_food.1=Canola Oil gives about 60 seconds of Hot Food time, Secret Chili Oil about 10 minutes, and Premium Chili Oil about 20 minutes. Remaining heat is shown on the food lore.
guide.kg.body.guide_hot_food.2=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%.
guide.kg.body.guide_hot_food.3=Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.guide_hot_food.4=A Secret Chili Oil Bucket is shapelessly crafted from 1 Canola Oil Bucket + 3 Red Chili Powder. All three oils can use the supported bucket, Big Vat, and Cookery Oil Pot transfer paths.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_redstone=Redstone: Speed
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_redstone.1=With 1–3 Redstone in the seasoning, eating it hot grants Speed I for a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_redstone.2=At 4 or more Redstone, it becomes Speed II.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_redstone.3=Houttuynia Powder can further extend this seasoning-effect duration.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_gunpowder=Gunpowder: Strength
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_gunpowder.1=With 1–3 Gunpowder in the seasoning, eating it hot grants Strength I for a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_gunpowder.2=At 4 or more Gunpowder, it becomes Strength II.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_gunpowder.3=Houttuynia Powder can further extend this seasoning-effect duration.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_houttuynia=Houttuynia Powder: Duration
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_houttuynia.1=Without Houttuynia Powder, regular seasoning effects have a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_houttuynia.2=Adding 1–3 Houttuynia Powder multiplies seasoning-effect duration by 2; 4 or more multiplies it by 4.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_houttuynia.3=Numb uses the same duration multiplier.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_totem=Totem Powder: Heavy Metal
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_totem.1=Add Totem Powder to seasoning and eat it hot to gain the Heavy Metal survival effect.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_totem.2=While active, otherwise-lethal damage consumes the survival effect and leaves you at 1 health.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_totem.3=After triggering, Heavy Metal Poisoning lasts about 10 minutes; using more of the same survival seasoning does not bypass that poisoned state.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_dragon=Dragon Egg Powder: Dragon Blood
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_dragon.1=Add Dragon Egg Powder to seasoning and eat it hot to gain Dragon Blood: increased maximum health plus a separate 2-point damage-absorption pool.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_dragon.2=1–3 Dragon Egg Powder uses the lower health-boost level; 4 or more uses the higher level.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_dragon.3=Houttuynia Powder extends Dragon Blood using the same ×2 / ×4 rule; Dragon Blood does not trigger after the food goes cold.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_pepper=Sichuan Pepper: Numb
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_pepper.1=Sichuan Pepper is one of the three base ingredients required to finish Special Seasoning.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_pepper.2=At 4 or more Sichuan Pepper in the same bottle, eating the food hot also triggers Numb for a base duration of about 45 seconds.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_pepper.3=Houttuynia Powder extends those 45 seconds using the same ×2 or ×4 rule.
guide.kg.name.guide_seasoning_limits=Seasoning capacity & cost
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_limits.1=Each bottle holds at most 8 ingredients, so “4 copies of a strengthening ingredient + the three base ingredients” already occupies 7 slots.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_limits.2=A finished bottle has 16 uses total. Seasoning a grill consumes as many uses as there are skewers on the grill.
guide.kg.body.guide_seasoning_limits.3=For example, if 3 skewers are on the grill but only 2 uses remain, seasoning is rejected rather than seasoning only two skewers.
guide.kg.name.guide_troubleshoot_grill=Why did the grill refuse?
guide.kg.body.guide_troubleshoot_grill.1=Cannot insert: confirm the grill is lit, still in the unoiled stage, and its 3 slots are not full.
guide.kg.body.guide_troubleshoot_grill.2=Cannot brush: at least 1 skewer must be present, the grill must still be unoiled, and the oil pot must have at least as many points as there are skewers.
guide.kg.body.guide_troubleshoot_grill.3=Cannot flip: oil first. Each flip has about a 1-second cooldown, and 4 flips are required.
guide.kg.body.guide_troubleshoot_grill.4=Cannot season: all 4 flips must be complete, the batch must not already be seasoned, and the bottle must have at least one use per skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_troubleshoot_grill.5=Cannot extract: a normal cooked batch must be seasoned first. An overcooked batch can be extracted directly with an empty hand.
guide.kg.name.guide_overcook_break=Breaking a grill mid-process
guide.kg.body.guide_overcook_break.1=Break the grill while still unoiled: skewers are returned in their raw state where possible.
guide.kg.body.guide_overcook_break.2=Break it after all 4 flips and successful seasoning: the batch is treated as cooked.
guide.kg.body.guide_overcook_break.3=Break it after overcooking: the batch becomes Dark Grilling.
guide.kg.body.guide_overcook_break.4=Break it during other incomplete post-oil stages: the contents become Mysterious Skewers.
guide.kg.name.guide_storage_heat=Hot-stack sorting
guide.kg.body.guide_storage_heat.1=Hot skewers do not freely merge with cold skewers or stacks whose remaining heat is very different.
guide.kg.body.guide_storage_heat.2=Sneak-use a Chest, Trapped Chest, or Barrel with an empty hand to sort skewers. Hot stacks only merge when their remaining Hot Food time differs by at most 5 minutes.
guide.kg.body.guide_storage_heat.3=Merged heat is a count-weighted average, so one fresh skewer cannot instantly refresh a whole old stack.
guide.kg.name.guide_secret_skewer=Secret Skewers
guide.kg.body.guide_secret_skewer.1=Three skewerable ingredients that do not match a fixed recipe become a Secret Skewer, storing the actual ingredients and creator information.
guide.kg.body.guide_secret_skewer.2=Secret Skewer nutrition is calculated from the actual edible ingredients rather than a fixed table; duplicate ingredients reduce the final nutrition yield.
guide.kg.body.guide_secret_skewer.3=An uncooked Secret Skewer can be sneak-disassembled. Once cooked, it retains the ingredient information used for nutrition.
guide.kg.name.guide_ordinary_challenge=The “Ordinary” Skewer warning
guide.kg.body.guide_ordinary_challenge.1=The “Ordinary” Skewer recipe is Poisonous Potato → Spider Eye → Pufferfish. It has no normal raw-to-cooked conversion.
guide.kg.body.guide_ordinary_challenge.2=Eating it directly triggers a lethal challenge; without Invincible, you die.
guide.kg.body.guide_ordinary_challenge.3=If you first gain Invincible from a Golden Skewer, the challenge consumes Invincible and randomly resolves as Strongest Shield or Strongest Spear. Only the Shield outcome blocks the lethal result.
guide.kg.name.guide_cold_houttuynia=Cold Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.guide_cold_houttuynia.1=Sneak at a Crafting Table with at least 3 Houttuynia in the main hand and a Cookery Oil Pot containing Premium Chili Oil in the off hand.
guide.kg.body.guide_cold_houttuynia.2=Crafting consumes 3 Houttuynia and 2 Premium Chili Oil points; any remaining oil stays in the pot.
guide.kg.body.guide_cold_houttuynia.3=Cold Houttuynia grants about 60 seconds of Fire Resistance when eaten.
guide.kg.name.guide_world_oil=Oil in the world
guide.kg.body.guide_world_oil.1=All three Grilling oil buckets can be placed into the world as fluids. A source flows downward first, then horizontally, using 8 visual levels.
guide.kg.body.guide_world_oil.2=An empty bucket can collect an oil source, and a Cookery Oil Pot can also take matching oil directly from a source.
guide.kg.body.guide_world_oil.3=On Bedrock these oils are script-simulated, so they do not promise every vanilla water/lava interaction. When an oil bucket is used on a Big Vat or Cookery Oil Pot, the container interaction takes priority.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_beef=Beef Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_beef.1=Ingredient order: Beef Chunks → Red Chili → Beef Chunks
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_beef.2=Cooked effect: Strength · base 10 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_pork_belly=Pork Belly Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_pork_belly.1=Ingredient order: Raw Pork Belly → Green Chili → Raw Pork Belly
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_pork_belly.2=Cooked effect: Vigor · base 30 seconds; suppresses hunger/saturation loss while sprinting.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_chicken_skin=Chicken Skin Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_chicken_skin.1=Ingredient order: Chicken Skin → Chicken Skin
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_chicken_skin.2=Cooked effect: Speed · base 20 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_mid_wing=Mid-Wing Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_mid_wing.1=Ingredient order: Chicken Wing → Red Chili → Chicken Wing
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_mid_wing.2=Cooked effect: Mustard · base 45 seconds; creepers within about 6 blocks are pushed away.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_squid_tentacle=Squid Tentacle Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.1=Ingredient order: Squid Tentacle → Squid Tentacle → Squid Tentacle
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.2=Cooked effect: Water Breathing · base 30 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_fish=Fish Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_fish.1=Ingredient order: Cod / Salmon / Tropical Fish / Pufferfish (choose 1)
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_fish.2=Cooked effect: Tundra Strider · base 30 seconds; faster on snow/ice and helps with Powder Snow.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet=Sweet Potato Sheet Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.1=Ingredient order: Raw Sweet Potato Sheet → Minced Houttuynia → Minced Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.2=Cooked effect: Preservation · base 45 seconds; removes hunger/poison/nausea-style penalties from dangerous foods.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_potato_slice=Potato Slice Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_potato_slice.1=Ingredient order: Potato Slice → Potato Slice → Potato Slice
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_potato_slice.2=Cooked effect: Warmth · base 30 seconds; can regenerate health while near heat sources.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_caterpillar=Caterpillar Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_caterpillar.1=Ingredient order: Caterpillar
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_caterpillar.2=Cooked effect: Flatulence · base 15 seconds; starting to sneak produces an upward impulse.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_mushroom=Mushroom Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_mushroom.1=Ingredient order: Brown/Red Mushroom → Carrot Dice → Brown/Red Mushroom
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_mushroom.2=Cooked effect: Night Vision · base 30 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_bun_slice=Bun Slice Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_bun_slice.1=Ingredient order: Raw Mantou Slice → Raw Mantou Slice → Raw Mantou Slice
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_bun_slice.2=No extra fixed cooked effect; it mainly provides its food value and Hot Food benefits.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_ender_pearl=Ender Pearl Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_ender_pearl.1=Ingredient order: Ender Pearl → Beetroot → Ender Pearl
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_ender_pearl.2=Cooked effect: Projectile Dodge · base 30 seconds; projectile hits are cancelled with a short teleport attempt, consuming about 10 seconds each time.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_meatball=Meatball Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_meatball.1=Ingredient order: Raw Meatball → Raw Meatball → Raw Meatball
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_meatball.2=Cooked effect: Strength · base 10 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_slime=Slime Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_slime.1=Ingredient order: Slimeball → Houttuynia → Slimeball
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_slime.2=Cooked effect: Hinder · base 45 seconds; your melee hits inflict Slowness II for about 5 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_meat_and_bone=Meat and Bone Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_meat_and_bone.1=Ingredient order: Raw Cut Small Meat → Bone → Raw Cut Small Meat
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_meat_and_bone.2=Cooked effect: Vigor · base 20 seconds; suppresses hunger/saturation loss while sprinting.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_fried_egg=Fried Egg Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_fried_egg.1=Ingredient order: Fried Egg → Fried Egg
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_fried_egg.2=Cooked effect: Sulfur · base 60 seconds; repels phantoms within roughly 8 blocks horizontally and 16 vertically.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_gluten=Gluten Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_gluten.1=Ingredient order: Raw Dough → Raw Dough
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_gluten.2=Cooked effect: Haste · base 30 seconds.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_lamb=Lamb Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_lamb.1=Ingredient order: Raw Lamb Chops → Cookery Oil → Raw Lamb Chops
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_lamb.2=Cooked effect: Warmth · base 45 seconds; can regenerate health while near heat sources.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_golden=Golden Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_golden.1=Ingredient order: Golden Apple → Totem of Undying → Golden Carrot
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_golden.2=Cooked effect: Invincible · base 10 seconds; most ordinary damage is cancelled. It is also used for the “Ordinary” Skewer challenge.
guide.kg.name.guide_recipe_ordinary=“Ordinary” Skewer
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_ordinary.1=Ingredient order: Poisonous Potato → Spider Eye → Pufferfish
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_ordinary.2=Special skewer: no raw→cooked conversion. Eating it triggers a lethal challenge; read Advanced & Troubleshooting first.
